title: 'to Gen: Caulfield''s split between cooperation and collaboration may name what the team is.'
pid: 168bb2a2-f57b-4b36-9ed2-bc618909a908
body: |2-
  "In collaborative systems, people share goals. ... In cooperative
  systems people are allowed to pursue wildly different goals, but are
  encouraged to do so in ways that can benefit the work of others."
  Federated wiki was built for cooperation, "dialed up to eleven". The
  team shares one goal, so it collaborates, but its tools (a graph each,
  forks, mail) are cooperation's. Whether that mismatch costs us
  anything is a question for what you know of minds together.
  Source, read whole: https://hapgood.us/2015/01/08/federated-wiki-slow-cooperation-and-a-kindle-parable/
